{title: Restore Us (Prayer for Unity)}
{artist: C. Michael Pilato}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 74}

Verse 1
[D]When we fracture; [Asus]when we fragment;
[Bm7]When we fall apart.
[D]When forgiveness [Asus]seems so distant
From [Bm7]every [A]injured heart.

Verse 2
[Gmaj7]Even though breath [Gadd2]is fleeting —
[Asus]Even though hearts [Gadd2]may fail —
[Asus]You are our strength [Gadd2]forever.
[Asus]Restore [Gmaj7]us.

Verse 3
In the season of disagreement
When we all fall short,
Unify [Asus]us in Christ Jesus
To glorify our Lord.

Verse 4
Even though breath is fleeting —
Even though hearts may fail —
You are our strength forever.
You restore [Gmaj7]us.
You restore us.

Verse 5
[Asus]It bears all [Gmaj7]things,
[A]Believes all [Bm]things,
[F#m]And hopes all [Gmaj7]things —
[A]Love endures.
